00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:04.190 align:start position:0%
Goldman Sachs is planning a round of  company-wide layoffs this month joining  the growing list of major corporations  and large companies who've done the same  out of fear of a looming recession the  investment bank usually lays off one to  five percent of its workers every year  as part of annual performance reviews  but suspended the program during the  pandemic here's a look at some of the  other big names that have been trimming  their Workforce this summer 2500  employees of the online used car seller  carvana received an email from CEO Ernie  Garcia saying they would be let go that  was 12 percent of the company's  Workforce about 1 100 coinbase employees  learned they had been laid off after  losing access to their work emails  marking an 18 reduction in the crypto  company's staff CEO Brian Armstrong said  the move was essential to staying  healthy during this economic downturn JP  Morgan Chase America's largest bank laid  off and reassigned more than one  thousand of its over 270 000 employees  citing Rising mortgage rates and  increased inflation real estate firm Max  announced plans to lay off 17 percent of  its Workforce by the end of 2022. the  company's staged goal is bringing in 100  million dollars in annual mortgage  related Revenue by 2028. Tesla laid off  229 employees mostly in its autopilot  Division and shut down its office in San  Mateo California  7-Eleven cut 880 U.S corporate jobs just  over a year after it completed a 21  billion dollar deal to purchase Speedway  Shopify cut 1 000 employees or 10  percent of its Workforce after  determining demand for online shopping  during the pandemic has leveled off  online crypto brokerage Robinhood cut 23  percent of its staff with CEO Vlad  tennis setting a drop in trading  activity High inflation and a broad  crypto market crash the company had  already laid off nine percent of its  full-time employees in April Ford  announced it will let go about 3 000  office and contract employees to cut  spending as it transitions to producing  electric vehicles  snap CEO Evan Spiegel announced in a  memo that the social media company will  lay off 1280 employees or 20 percent as  the company is facing a lower rate of  Revenue growth the company's stock price  has plummeted nearly 80 percent since  earlier this year and finally Investment  Banking giant Credit Suisse could cut as  many as 5 000 jobs as the Scandal hit  Bank seeks to turn around its reputation  and reduce costs  [Music]
 

